<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  How much a to-do list (todo_peer) is allowed to hold, as the host tells a copy of it:
  `values`, the most values its registers hold (a change that would give a register that
  holds no value one more value past it is refused). A 0 is no limit.

  The limit is the host's to give a list because a list is built with the room it has
  (`sce:limit`, the bounds a deployment chooses) and what a list holds is a plan's: one
  account's calendar is given less than another's out of the same build. A person's copy
  refuses a change of its own, whole, before anything is stamped or sent, and takes in
  what the others sent without asking: they were judged where they were made. So the
  number is given to every copy alike, and kept below the bound the list is built with by
  what the people of one list can write at once before they have seen each other's.

  The changes a copy holds not yet stable are not the list's to count: the layer that
  delivers them keeps them, and its room is the deployment's (docs/adr/0085, section 3).
  The rooms of the tombstones and of the digest went with them; a host that still sends
  `history` or `digest` changes nothing, a key the schema does not declare being stepped
  over where the event is read.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0"
       sce:kind="event-schema"
       name="todo_room"
       sce:event-name="todo.room">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="values" sce:type="uint32" sce:direction="in"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
